\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The unified graph ontology (schematic). Seven label classes and eight relation types share one namespace; there is no separate episodic, skill, or intention store. Cross-space links (blue, corridor-routed) are the core capability: the \texttt  {leads-to} edge from \texttt  {action experience} to \texttt  {change} (weight = confidence) is the product of the write-back pipeline (Section~\ref {sec:arch-wb}); \texttt  {gap} points to an entity to inject activation; \texttt  {event} carries a negative-polarity slot edge (red dashed) suppressing the entity (Section~\ref {sec:arch-persist}).}}{3}{figure.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{fig:ontology}{{1}{3}{The unified graph ontology (schematic). Seven label classes and eight relation types share one namespace; there is no separate episodic, skill, or intention store. Cross-space links (blue, corridor-routed) are the core capability: the \texttt {leads-to} edge from \texttt {action experience} to \texttt {change} (weight = confidence) is the product of the write-back pipeline (Section~\ref {sec:arch-wb}); \texttt {gap} points to an entity to inject activation; \texttt {event} carries a negative-polarity slot edge (red dashed) suppressing the entity (Section~\ref {sec:arch-persist})}{figure.caption.1}{}}
